        "stages": {
            "$comment": "Cross-step landscape uniqueness is NOT expressed here, deliberately. A Kargo Stage name is <platform>-<service>-<landscape> (diene-platform.stageName), so a landscape repeated in two steps renders two Stages with the SAME name in one namespace. JSON Schema cannot state that: the uniqueItems on a parallel stageStep compares whole member VALUES inside a SINGLE step, so \"pichu\" and {landscape: pichu} are distinct items to it, and it cannot see across steps at all. Writing a schema keyword that appears to cover this would be a vacuous guard. The invariant is enforced fail-closed at render by diene-platform.assertPipeline (templates/_helpers.tpl), which also refuses a soak on the first step, and is proven non-vacuous by scripts/validate/fleet.sh dag / dag-negative.",
